  "text": {
    "work": "work",
    "card": "Turn an indexed crank, rigid connecting rod and straight-guided slider.",
    "slider_crank": "slider crank",
    "linkage": "connecting rod linkage",
    "wrong_phase": "Choose the turn matching the current phase.",
    "free_hand": "Put down an object so a hand is free for the rear shaft control.",
    "howto_turn": "Use the forward or backward offer matching the current phase at the rear shaft control. Blue C is the crank, gold R the rigid rod and green S the slider. Forward turns counterclockwise viewed from the front, in sixteen 22.5 degree steps; the pale crank index moves against four fixed red references. The orange crank pin and lavender slider pin span the separated crank and rod planes. A 120 mm crank radius and unchanged 360 mm pin-center rod give 240 mm slider travel along fixed rails. Red marks above the guide show both travel endpoints. Only sixteen endpoint configurations are represented: the rod is not resized, but no intermediate constraint closure, physical force, torque, dead-point drive, engine, pump, output, loose-item custody or team authority is simulated. Turning through a dead point is an indexed depiction, not a force demonstration."
  },
